# Line endings, decided here rather than by whatever core.autocrlf a machine
# happens to have set.
#
# Why this file exists: several tests read their own source with include_str!
# and search it for newline-delimited patterns, for example
# "\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn settings_paths". Those searches only match on
# LF. With core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone or a new git worktree gets CRLF,
# the searches stop matching, and two tests fail in a checkout that is
# byte-identical in git to one where they pass. That happened on 2026-09-09
# and cost an hour to diagnose, because the code was never the problem.
#
# So: text files are LF in the working tree as well as in the repository.
# Windows tooling here (PowerShell, Inno Setup, cargo, node) all read LF fine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything Windows genuinely wants as CRLF.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png  binary
*.bmp  binary
*.ico  binary
*.iso  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.zip  binary
*.bin  binary
*.raw  binary
*.dds  binary
*.xdelta binary
*.rebornroster binary
